From: pdx203 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: bridge: metal2vulkan patch 0037, elide a landscape copy back a later one supersedes

Carries bridge/patches/0037-rotated-copy-back-elided.patch. QuartzCore draws two full-frame passes into its landscape framebuffer
per frame, in one command buffer; each copied back the whole rotated frame, and only the second reached the display. A copy back
is now an indirect dispatch from a slot of the texture's, and the later one zeroes the earlier's workgroups before submission where
no command read or wrote the plane in between (encoders that may be encoded again, fence updates and signals elide nothing).

